```sql
--Description / Thinking process:
-- Objective: illustrate how to calculate an exponential moving average (EMA, α = 0.2)
-- for patent‑filing counts over the years for one CPC level‑5 prefix that is known to exist
-- in the dataset (here we use ‘G06F3’—“Computer input/​output arrangements”).
--
-- Steps
-- 1. yearly_counts  – Aggregate the number of publications per filing year that have
--    ‘G06F3’ as the first CPC code (array index 0).  Derive the year by
--    FLOOR(filing_date/10000).  Keep only rows with a positive filing date and
--    a non‑null application number.
-- 2. ranked_yearly  – Add a dense rank (rank_idx) ordered from the most‑recent year
--    downward.  Having rank_idx as a material column prevents any “window‑inside‑window”
--    nesting later.
-- 3. ema_parts      – Compute two running sums with separate window functions:
--      • Numerator: Σ [pub_cnt × 0.8^(rank_idx‑1)]
--      • Denominator: Σ [0.8^(rank_idx‑1)]
--    where 0.8 = (1‑α).
-- 4. Final SELECT   – Divide numerator by denominator to obtain EMA for each year,
--    ordered chronologically; show the first 20 rows.

WITH yearly_counts AS (
    SELECT
        FLOOR(p."filing_date" / 10000)             AS "year",
