Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns, their potential usage, and basic conditions  
• PUBLICATIONS."cpc" (VARIANT): contains the CPC symbols for every publication – flatten it and keep the very first entry (“index” = 0) to obtain “the first CPC code”.  
• PUBLICATIONS."filing_date" (NUMBER): yyyymmdd; use it for the filing‑year (FLOOR("filing_date"/10000)) and require > 0.  
• PUBLICATIONS."application_number" (TEXT): make sure it is NOT NULL/NOT '' so that we only keep records with a genuine application number.  
• PUBLICATIONS."application_kind" (TEXT): optional extra filter if we want only patent‑type “A/U/F/W…”, but left open in the examples.  
• CPC_DEFINITION."symbol" (TEXT): full CPC symbol – join to the CPC symbol (or to its truncated group code) coming from PUBLICATIONS.  
• CPC_DEFINITION."titleFull" (TEXT): full English title of the CPC area – to be shown in the final list.  
• CPC_DEFINITION."level" (FLOAT): filter to level = 5 so that we work on CPC level‑5 groups.  

Typical conditions  
WHERE "filing_date" IS NOT NULL  
      AND "filing_date" > 0  
      AND "application_number" IS NOT NULL  
      AND "application_number" <> ''  

